I think it is making some assumptions about the reader's dialect of English=
. In American pronunciation for instance, "joke" and "note" indeed have a s=
ound which could only be the "o" in Lojban. It is not necessarily the prefe=
rred Lojban "o" sound, but it is too far from "a" and "au" for any confusio=
n. (This is one of the advantages of not having very many vowels!)

